<footer class="af-summary"><h2 data-factory-copy="summary">The factory in one minute</h2><p data-factory-copy="summaryText">Electricity reaches the data center through the grid, substation and transformers. Distribution supplies GPU racks; high-speed networking connects the cluster. Liquid cooling removes heat, and software schedules the work. The useful outputs include text, video, agents and robot actions. Revenue follows when customers pay for those outputs.</p><p class="af-boundary" data-factory-copy="boundary">Conceptual teaching animation. Equipment counts, activity lights and timings illustrate the process; they are not capacity, utilization or revenue measurements.</p></footer>
